{"type":"text","text":"Done. Mapping sheet 1 for Super Mario Bros., World 1-1 first screen, is recorded and promoted.\n\n## Small Mario — metasprite\n`list_sprites` (paused, `game_mode $0770=1`) returned **one sprite-palette-4 cluster of 8 OAM entries** — the 2-wide × 4-tall (16×32) stack SMB emits for both sizes. Only the bottom two rows are drawn; the top two are the blank tile `$FC` padding. Screen anchor x=40, y=193.\n\n| OAM | tile | offset | flip |\n|----|------|--------|------|\n| 1 | $FC | (+0,−16) | no |\n| 2 | $FC | (+8,−16) | no |\n| 3 | $FC | (+0,−8) | no |\n| 4 | $FC | (+8,−8) | no |\n| 5 | $3A | (+0,0) | no |\n| 6 | $37 | (+8,0) | no |\n| 7 | $4F | (+0,+8) | no |\n| 8 | $4F | (+8,+8) | **h-flip** |\n\nRecorded as sprite `small_mario`.\n\n## His colors — sprite palette 4\n`[34,22,39,24]` = slot 0 `$22` periwinkle (transparent for sprites), slot 1 `$16` red, slot 2 `$27` orange, slot 3 `$18` olive.\n- **Proof:** `write_palette` 4/1 → `$2C` cyan, `step_frame` 1, screenshot: cap and shirt turned cyan while face stayed orange and outline stayed olive. `get_pixel_color` (45,193)=`$2C`, (44,196)=`$27`, (43,196)=`$18`. `clear_palette_overrides` restored red.\n- So slot 1 = cap + shirt/body, slot 2 = face/skin, slot 3 = dark linework (outline, hair, eye, shoes).\n\n## The bush\n`get_region` object mode at (222,199) returned connected BG palette-0 pixels (slots 1,2,3), bbox (190,192)–(247,207), CHR `0x125/0x135/0x136/0x137/0x138`. Each recorded with table 1 and group `bush`:\n- **$135** bush left end (rounded lower-left)\n- **$136** bush top bump left half\n- **$136/$137** pair = one 16px bump (three across, nametable row 24)\n- **$137** bush top bump right half\n- **$138** bush right end (rounded lower-right)\n- **$125** bush bottom fill (solid green, nametable row 25 cols 24–29)\n\nAll 7 discoveries were promoted into `mappings/sha1-33d23c2f…json` (now 23 tiles, 7 palettes, 1 sprite). Emulator is running again."}
